# Lessons

## User Specified Lessons

- You have a python venv in ./venv (create if needed). Check `which uv` first; if available use `uv pip install`, else `pip`.
- For multiline commit messages, write the message to a file and use `git commit -F <filename>`, then delete the file. Include "[Cursor] " in commit messages and PR titles.

## Cursor learned

- This repo (GigaLearnCPP) was developed on MSVC; GCC needed: Timer clock fix, include-path case fixes, -fPIC on static libs, no std::iterator, cxxabi demangling.
- libtorch 2.x requires CMake >= 3.18; CPU build for Linux: https://download.pytorch.org/libtorch/cpu/libtorch-cxx11-abi-shared-with-deps-2.5.1%2Bcpu.zip -> extract to GigaLearnCPP/libtorch (gitignored).
- On this VM, `c++` is clang++ without libstdc++ dev files: always configure with -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=g++.
- `configure_file(... COPY)` is invalid CMake; must be COPYONLY.
- `torch::tensor(std::vector<T>)` is ~2.7x slower than `from_blob(...).clone()` for big buffers (measured).
- gather()/index_copy_ in libtorch require kInt64 index tensors (runtime error otherwise).
- Test CMake globs need CONFIGURE_DEPENDS or a manual reconfigure to pick up new files.
- tmux sessions get reaped in this environment; run long builds as foreground Shell commands with big block_until_ms instead.
- Collision meshes: synthetic box mesh can be generated for smoke tests (struct: int32 numTris, int32 numVerts, tris as 3x int32, verts as 3x float, little-endian, .cmf in collision_meshes/soccar/).
- rlgym-ppo interop: GigaLearn model files are POLICY.lt/CRITIC.lt/SHARED_HEAD.lt (torch::save archives, loadable with torch.jit.load in Python).

# Scratchpad

## Task: Add SAC with discrete actions as a second learning algorithm (with configuration) — branch cursor/add-discrete-sac-7a1d

### Design (decided after codebase audit)
- Algorithm: SAC-Discrete (Christodoulou 2019). Policy = same categorical masked-softmax nets as PPO
  (shared_head optional + policy) so InferUnit / PolicyVersionManager / skill tracker / RLBot stay compatible.
- Twin Q nets ("q1"/"q2", obs -> numActions) + Polyak-averaged target copies (saved without optims).
- Entropy temperature alpha: fixed or auto-tuned (log-alpha param + Adam) toward target entropy = scale * log(numActions).
- Off-policy: new ReplayBuffer (preallocated circular tensors, uniform sampling). Transitions derived from the
  existing collection loop's Trajectory data (states/actions/rewards/terminals + truncation next-states/masks).
- Learner gets cfg.algorithm (PPO | SAC) + cfg.sac (SACLearnerConfig). Collection loop shared; consumption branches.
- Shared code extracted: PolicyInference (MakePolicyModels/InferProbs/InferActions/ComputeEntropy), MetricAccum,
  AlgoLearner interface (device + policy access) used by PolicyVersionManager.
- SAC path skips GAE/returnStat (no reward normalization; alpha absorbs scale). standardizeObs works (stale-stats caveat documented).
- RUNNING_STATS.json gains "algorithm" field; mismatch = clear error. Transfer learn + guiding policy stay PPO-only (guarded).

